{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "control": "D0"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 131, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling an empty edge 5 brings node 2's computation back into the output, a bigger gain than swapping out an existing op there."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a residual input-to-output path where none existed helps more than replacing an op that already carried signal to the output."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 5 absent, node 3 has fewer inputs, so removing the skip on edge 3 hurts more."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "With edge 2 absent, node 1 feeds fewer downstream paths, so cutting edge 0 loses less."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 5 absent, node 2 never reaches the output, so a conv on edge 1 has almost no effect instead of a positive one."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 0 absent, node 1 receives no input, so a conv on edge 2 contributes nothing."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a conv on edge 4 with pooling normally hurts, but with edge 0 absent node 1 is dead and the swap barely matters."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 5 also absent, removing edge 4 leaves only the skip on edge 3 reaching the output, so accuracy collapses."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "With edge 0 absent, edge 2 carries no signal, so removi